<title>USA: PLC Systems says study supports Heart Laser.</title>
<headline>PLC Systems says study supports Heart Laser.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKLIN, Mass. 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>PLC Systems Inc said a clinical study supported the company's Heart Laser as an adjunct to minimally invasive bypass surgery.</p>
<p>The company said it presented results of the study at the American College of Cardiology's Annual Scientific Session.</p>
<p>The results showed that 92 percent of 56 patients who used the Heart Laser with the surgery did not experience chest pain 12 months later. That percentage of people also had a higher tolerance for exercise, the company said.</p>
